Once upon a time, in the lush and dangerous Stranglethorn Vale, a Gnome Warlock named Zephyr set out on a quest to gather rare ingredients for his alchemy. His Succubus pet, named Sylph, was a loyal companion, but Zephyr found himself more often than not using his Succubus to scout ahead and gather information. This was because Sylph had a unique ability: she could cast "Shadowstep," a spell that allowed her to teleport a short distance, making her a valuable scout and a formidable ally in the dense jungle.

Zephyr's story ends with him successfully completing his quest and returning home, his Succubus pet Sylph always by his side, though she was rarely seen in combat. The answer to the riddle is that Succubus's Shadowstep ability makes them more common and useful in exploration and scouting, overshadowing their combat prowess. [end of text]


